WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.227
A Common Table Expression begins with WITH.

00:00:03.227 --> 00:00:07.897
Think of it as a named intermediate relation inside one statement.

00:00:07.897 --> 00:00:11.542
The first stage can summarize or clean the source.

00:00:11.542 --> 00:00:14.877
A later stage can join or enrich that result.

00:00:14.877 --> 00:00:18.207
The final SELECT consumes the prepared data.

00:00:18.207 --> 00:00:23.197
Naming the stages helps you reason about the transformation one step at a time.

00:00:23.197 --> 00:00:29.762
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:37.017
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a new

00:00:37.017 --> 00:00:44.843
block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
